<h2>Select — per-component projection</h2>
<p>
    <code>Select</code> transforms the cached value before it is published to <code>Data</code>.
    It is per query, so two components can project one entry differently — the cache always stores
    the raw value.
</p>

<h2>PlaceholderData</h2>
<p>
    Rendered as <code>Data</code> while the first fetch runs and the cache is empty; never written
    to the cache. Use it for skeleton rows that are typed like real data.
</p>

<Callout Type="Callout.CalloutType.Warning" Title="Keyed joins drop parameters">
    <p>A same-key <code>Execute</code> made while one is in flight <em>joins</em> that execution:
        the second call's parameters are dropped and no supersede happens. Don't reuse one key
        across calls whose parameters differ — omit the key to get supersede semantics instead.</p>
</Callout>

